{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Elohim be gracious to us</b> — like: חנונו אתם (grant us), like: אשר חנן (who showed favor)." "And the sense of 'may He bless us' is that He adds beyond that which He grants us." "And the sense of 'may He make His face shine' — that we find favor in His eyes, as we ask of Him."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 67, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:57.298607015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}